+# Switch build notices
+
+OpenRealm is MIT licensed; see LICENSE and individual vendored dependency notices.
+The project is not affiliated with Blizzard Entertainment or Nintendo.
+
+The binary statically links the following libraries from devkitPro packages:
+
+- SDL2 2.28.5: zlib license, https://github.com/devkitPro/SDL
+- Mesa 20.1.0: MIT and component-specific permissive licenses, https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa
+- libdrm_nouveau 1.0.1: MIT, https://github.com/devkitPro/libdrm_nouveau
+- libnx 4.12.0: ISC, https://github.com/switchbrew/libnx
+- zlib 1.3.1: zlib license, https://zlib.net/zlib_license.html
+- GCC 16.1.0 runtime/libstdc++: GPLv3 with GCC Runtime Library Exception,
+  https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/libstdc++/manual/license.html
+- Newlib 4.6.0.20260123: component-specific permissive licenses,
+  https://sourceware.org/newlib/COPYING.NEWLIB
+
+These are community homebrew libraries, not proprietary Nintendo SDK binaries.
+No retail game data or keysets are included. Test fixtures originate from the
+upstream source tree and are not loaded as a replacement retail installation.
